# Frontend build-time configuration.
#
# Both variables are OPTIONAL and both are read at BUILD time, not at runtime:
# Vite substitutes `import.meta.env.VITE_*` into the bundle when it compiles.
# Changing either one in a hosting dashboard therefore has no effect until the
# site is rebuilt — a redeploy, not a restart.
#
# Local development needs neither. The dev server proxies /api and /ws to
# http://localhost:4000 (see vite.config.ts), so `npm run dev` works unset.

# Absolute origin of the backend, including the protocol and with no trailing
# slash or path. Unset means "same origin as the page", which is the previous
# behaviour and what the dev proxy relies on.
#
# Set this whenever the frontend is served from a different origin than the
# backend — a Vercel-hosted dashboard talking to a Render-hosted backend, say.
# The backend must also list this frontend's origin in its own CORS_ORIGIN, or
# the REST calls are blocked and the WebSocket handshake is refused with 403;
# see "Allowed Origins" in the root README.
# VITE_API_URL=https://netpulse-backend-6myk.onrender.com

# Origin for the /ws WebSocket. Almost never needed: the backend serves the
# socket on the same port as the REST API, so this is derived from
# VITE_API_URL by swapping the protocol (http -> ws, https -> wss). Set it only
# if the socket is genuinely served somewhere else. The /ws path is appended
# automatically, and a value that already ends in /ws is left alone.
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://netpulse-backend-6myk.onrender.com
